# L §2.4 Inside a section (tally 2.1.7 R9, issue #148; the builder's SR-B5, pick P40): "a place keyed by things
# (`konto[ana]`) is one key, sorted as things are"; at a position whose index isn't loaded keys sort by kind first,
# a thing's name ranking as a key. So a keyed place sorts among the plain things in their text order. refcore 2.1.7
# kept 2.1.6's rank for it (that of a month-day under the kind-first order) and printed every keyed place first.
=== options reprint
=== s.tally
scenario s over m
  tally 2
  from 2026-01-01

version w
  cite c
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  opening[wcash[ike]] = 1 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[marek] = 2 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[gotowka] = 3 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[wunits[ike]] = 4 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[konto] = 5 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
